# Site information architecture

This is a career/job site. Each URL has one job. Do not restate current-role evidence across pages.

| URL | Job |
|---|---|
| `/` | Identity, proof chips, selected work, one delivery snapshot, contact |
| `/kit` | Recruiter leave-behind (open-to, evidence links, PDF) |
| `/work` | Evidence. Current-role outcomes live only in the Jacobs case study |
| `/about` | Person: career, research, a short music coda |
| `/research/global-flood-mapping` | Canonical GeoHorizons publication page |
| `/delivery` | Forwardable written bar. Do not CTA it from About |
| `/now` | This-month status and booking — not a bio |
| `/resume` | Complete record |

Canonical copy: `person.bio` (identity), `facts.php` (scale chips), Jacobs case study (current evidence).

## Music

Keep music tight on `/about` (“Beyond the work”). Do not add `/music` or put music in the primary nav. No engineering/music metaphors.
